{
  "_doc": "Environment-aware gunshot tails (build_tails.py). REAL RECORDINGS ONLY: every file is a time-sliced, EQ'd, faded (and for some open-air variants layered) cut of a real recording of gunfire in that kind of space - nothing is synthesised, no impulse response is generated or convolved. Sources are paths relative to C:\\tb\\audio-src (never committed): sonniss/ = the Pole Position indoor / outdoor gun acoustics libraries and Audiobeast's London Warehouse library, tsp/ = the Tactical Shooter Pack. A layer is [shot onset + start_s, shot onset + end_s] of its source (t = the shot's approximate time in the source, refined to the blast's first sample; packs' own shots are found automatically). The file is timelined from the shot instant (leading silence = start_s) like the generic fire_tail, so it starts together with the close layer; start_s skips the direct sound (the close layer carries it). Every output records its source slices in the manifest `sources` list; check_audio.py fails a tail without one. Classes: indoor_small = Audiobeast small room (H&K 416) + Pole Position catacombs; indoor_large = Audiobeast medium warehouse (870 x8) + Pole Position long corridor; outdoor_urban = Pole Position valley behind buildings; outdoor_open = Pole Position big open area + forest road, layered with the pack's long With_Tail recordings for the long rolling decay.",
